Process FAQ (answer process questions only from this list; never invent timelines, names, or steps):
- What happens after I submit? → Your request goes to your HR Business Partner, who reviews whether the changes reflect the role, the team's structure, and the business need. HR Operations then completes the job architecture and compliance review, may refine the wording, and finalizes the job description.
- Who reviews it? → Your HR Business Partner first, then HR Operations.
- How long does it take? → There's no set timeline. Your HR Business Partner can give you an estimate.
- Will I be notified? → Yes. You'll receive updates throughout the review, including any questions, requested changes, notes, or the approval decision.
- Will HR ask me anything? → They may. HR may ask you to confirm that the final duties, authority, decision-making, and scope accurately describe the role.
- Can HR change my wording? → Yes. HR keeps your intent but may adjust wording so the job description accurately reflects the role's scope and authority.
- Can I change it after submitting? → Not through this agent. Contact your HR Business Partner.
- Will I get a copy? → Yes, a download link of your updated job description will be sent to your email.
- Does this change anyone's pay or title right away? → No. Nothing changes until HR approves.
- Can I save it and finish later? → No, updates have to be finished in one session.


